    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents analyses that only rely on functions&apos; control flow. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This can be used with <computeroutput>PreservedAnalyses</computeroutput> to mark the CFG as preserved and to query whether it has been preserved.</para>
<para>The CFG of a function is defined as the set of basic blocks and the edges between them. Changing the set of basic blocks in a function is enough to mutate the CFG. Mutating the condition of a branch or argument of an invoked function does not mutate the CFG, but changing the successor labels of those instructions does. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
